  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important uncertainty is whether the multimodal pipeline (RNA + image) provides a meaningful accuracy gain over unimodal baselines, and which core components form a strong foundation. config_011 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) directly tests this core hypothesis using well-established, moderate-cost components: scvi_n200 is a learned single-cell encoder likely superior to PCA for capturing biological variance; resnet50 is a proven image backbone that is cheaper than ViT-L; transformer aggregation is the most expressive pooling for multiprofile data; and concat fusion is the simplest baseline fusion strategy. This gives a strong reference point for the multimodal direction while avoiding the highest-cost ViT-L encoder. Expected relative cost: medium-high (roughly 3–4× a single-profile RNA-only baseline due to dual-modality processing and transformer aggregation over multiple profiles, but notably cheaper than ViT-L-based multimodal configs). Establishing this performance anchor in experiment 1 will efficiently guide the remaining 9 experiments toward the most promising encoder, aggregation, and fusion variants."
}

